# Mobile PWA — Netlify redirect rules.
#
# Bare URL → land directly in the installed-app view of app.html. This stops
# new visitors from seeing the design-preview mockup (all screens scrolled
# vertically), which they'd otherwise hit if they typed just the hostname.
#
# Old shape: https://agro-more-app.netlify.app/
#            → renders index.html, which is the design-preview, confusing.
# New shape: same URL silently rewrites to /app.html?mode=app, which is what
#            farmers actually use.
#
# The rewrite is server-side so the user URL stays "/" — they only ever see
# the clean hostname. 200! status forces rewrite (not 301 redirect) so the
# hash-routed app paths (#home-1 etc.) work without redirect loops.
/   /app.html?mode=app   200!
